      en: "The Port of Klaipėda is Lithuania's most vital logistical hub and one of the few ice-free ports in the northernmost part of the Baltic Sea. Situated at the mouth of the Curonian Lagoon, it functions as a primary gateway for trade between Western Europe, Scandinavia, and Eastern markets. Since Lithuania regained independence, the port has undergone extensive modernization, including dredging operations that allow it to accommodate massive Post-Panamax vessels. A strategic milestone was the 2014 opening of the 'Independence' LNG terminal, which fundamentally secured the country's energy independence. The port features specialized terminals for containers, Ro-Ro cargo, grain, and petroleum products. Beyond its economic weight, the port is a major regional employer and is increasingly focused on integrating green technologies to protect the sensitive Baltic Sea ecosystem.",
